* Chidō Inari (智童稲荷)

== Offerings ==
* Chigibako (木筥) – The chigibako is said either to have originated from using leftover materials (wooden planks called “chigi” that were used to make a rice container) at the time of the shrine’s construction or from the abbreviation of “mochiki” (a vessel for mounded rice cakes). Today, the chigibako—into which beans are placed—may be hung in a room to ward off lightning.
* Shiba Shinmei Ginger – At the time the shrine was founded, the surrounding area was known for its flourishing ginger fields. It is said that ginger was offered before the deity; thereafter, consuming the ginger removed from the altar became reputed to prevent colds, and during the annual festival ginger is again distributed.

== Cultural Properties ==
; Nagasawa Ashisetsu Painted Portrait (人物図)<ref name="長沢芦雪筆人物図"/>: Tangible Cultural Property (painting) designated by Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}
; Colored Paper Mount Hakonoyeizu by Tatebe Suso (建部巣兆筆)<ref name="紙本着色箱根詣図 建部巣兆筆"/>: Tangible Cultural Property (painting) designated by Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}
; Kagura Mask with “Kagura Mask Catalogue” attached<ref name="神楽面 付「神楽面目録」"/>: Tangible Cultural Property (sculpture) designated by Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}
; Kagura Mask: Registered Tangible Cultural Property (sculpture) in Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}
; Ashikaga Naoyoshi’s Teaching Document<ref name="足利直義御教書"/>: Tangible Cultural Property (ancient document) designated by Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}
; Kira Clan Red Seal Document<ref name="吉良氏朱印状"/>: Tangible Cultural Property (ancient document) designated by Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}
; Inaha Hanjūrō Chūji Letter<ref name="伊奈半十郎忠治書状"/>: Tangible Cultural Property (ancient document) designated by Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}
; Sacred Edict: Registered Tangible Cultural Property (ancient document) in Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}
; Document of the Bettō/Priests<ref name="別当・神主等申状 案"/>: Registered Tangible Cultural Property (ancient document) in Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}
; Bronze Lantern: Registered Tangible Cultural Property (historical material) in Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}
; The Power Stone of Shiba Daijingu<ref name="芝大神宮の力石"/>: Tangible Folk Cultural Property designated by Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}
; Hanchō of the Megumi Group: Registered Tangible Folk Cultural Property in Minato Ward {{sfn|港区立郷土歴史館}}

== Access ==
* 5‑minute walk from Hamamatsuchō Station on the {{ill|JR Yamanote Line|ja|山手線|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/JR Yamanote Line|qq=}} and {{ill|Keihin–Tōhoku Line|ja|京浜東北線|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Keihin–Tōhoku Line|qq=}} ({{ill|JR|ja|東日本旅客鉄道|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/JR|qq=}})
* 1‑minute walk from Daimon Station ({{ill|Daimon Station|ja|大門駅 (東京都)|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Daimon Station|qq=}}) on the Toei Asakusa Line ({{ill|Toei Subway|ja|東京都交通局|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Toei Subway|qq=}} – {{ill|Asakusa Line|ja|都営地下鉄浅草線|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Asakusa Line|qq=}} and {{ill|Oedo Line|ja|都営地下鉄大江戸線|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Oedo Line|qq=}})
* 5‑minute walk from Onarimon Station on the Toei Mita Line ({{ill|Toei Subway Mita Line|ja|都営地下鉄三田線|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Toei Subway Mita Line|qq=}})

